 Limit orders are the one cost lever available, but they are not free money. Live experiments on Binance found that maker fills are **adversely selected**: the orders that fill easily are the ones followed by adverse moves ([Albers et al., arXiv 2502.18625](https://arxiv.org/html/2502.18625v2)). Unfilled limit orders also miss the momentum days a trend rule exists to catch. A backtest that books every limit order at its limit price overstates the saving.
 
